# Spectrum v3 (`@adobe/react-spectrum` / `@react-spectrum/*`)

Applies to v3 packages only (not `@react-spectrum/s2` or `s2-*`).

## Building components

- Compose aria/stately (or shared `react-aria`) hooks; own DOM structure + Spectrum CSS only.
- Style via Spectrum CSS (`import styles from '@adobe/spectrum-css-temp/...'`) and style props (`useStyleProps`), not the S2 `style` macro.
- Public interaction handlers use **`onPress`**, not `onClick`.
- Localize UI chrome with `intlMessages` + `useLocalizedStringFormatter`.
- Put shared prop types in `@react-types` when they are part of the public API; document props with JSDoc.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Button onClick={handler} className="custom">Save</Button>

// ✅ GOOD
<Button variant="accent" onPress={handler}>Save</Button>
```

## Tests & stories

- Tests often need `<Provider theme={theme}>...</Provider>`.
- Stories live with the package; run v3 Storybook via `yarn start` (port 9003).

## Consumer docs

For app-facing v3 usage, see `rules/react-spectrum-v3.mdc`. For migrations to S2, see `rules/react-spectrum-v3-to-s2-migration.mdc`.
